  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 100 AM CDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\nThe dominant ridge of high pressure pivots westward by the \nweekend, allowing a weak frontal boundary to sneak south Saturday \ninto Sunday with a brief northerly wind shift and low to medium \n(20-35 percent) chance of rain Saturday night into Sunday \nafternoon with isolated thunderstorms possible. At this time, most\nQPF forecasts keep isolated amounts below one-tenth to one-\nquarter of an inch. The GFS and ECMWF briefly pop PWAT values \nabove 2 inches as the boundary swings south, above the 90th \npercentile for early August, but vary wildly on location and at \nleast do not stall the moisture. NBM probabilities remain low \n(below 15 percent) for any rainfall greater than one-half inch, \nmainly near Del Rio and Eagle Pass. With little confidence in \neither solution at this time, will stick to current POPs and QPF \nand continue to monitor trends into the end of the week. \n\nOtherwise, expect seasonal heat to carry into the first week of\nAugust, potentially down a couple of degrees from the end of this\nweek but still likely popping triple-digit Heat Indices. A\nModerate (level 2 of 4) to Major (level 3 of 4) Heat Risk persists\ninto mid-week, so heat safety messaging continues to be the\nprimary concern.",
